{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":63,"timestamp":"2026-07-11T21:56:27.526959772Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"66f52b44-3710-40c1-a7d8-ec78c4c0b185","title":"upstream-parity: show full PSP-ID hex + CPU codename in generation column (PSPTool #55)","description":"Upstream: https://github.com/PSPReverse/PSPTool/issues/55 -- OPEN, maintainer receptive.\n\nTable shows coarse 'Zen N'; low bytes of the PSP/zen-generation ID pin the exact SoC. Reporter wants the full ID hex (e.g. 0xBC0C0140) and ideally codename (Zen 3 (Cezanne)). Directly answers the #46 question and disambiguates combo/multi-generation images. coreboot publishes many full IDs so a PSP_ID->codename map is tractable.\n\nImpl: the full ID is already read during combo/tertiary parsing (directory.rs, cf. crosslink #51 step 3); carry it onto the directory and render hex + optional codename lookup in crates/psptool-ops/src/table.rs. Additive column -- guard the differential snapshots. See docs/upstream-issue-review.md.","priority":"low","parent_uuid":"525d7258-de71-4087-8d5a-f7dd155266b5","created_by":"tLiK"},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPscOVF8LCqNnpSIAmx6wu+I0K+xGblsIalVNTLbKaMxrJbnGB5+RgISRBkvtCAkFfgKB3T6vlmfYfSN6PIl6gQ="}
