{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":67,"timestamp":"2026-07-11T21:57:44.654852592Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"d691bf6c-5bf6-47f0-a0ca-d64fb76b0695","comment_uuid":"5e2c838e-ab2c-4ef0-8760-3c99b8c62b96","author":"tLiK","content":"Plan: mirror directory.py:85-99 in walk_directories (directory.rs). For PSP/BIOS entries where entry_type.is_tertiary_directory_pointer() (0x48/0x4A): resolve the entry offset exactly like the secondary path (dir_mode.resolve_with_entry) to locate the 32-byte block (upstream entry.file_offset(), directory.py:163), read block[16:20] as the real L2 offset (directory.py:88), apply the ROM addr_mask via AddressMode::PhysicalX86.resolve (mirrors from_offset 'rom_offset &= addr_mask', directory.py:105), then reuse the SAME parse_at/visit/dedup machinery to enqueue the $PL2. Unknown generation id does NOT gate recursion (upstream only warns, directory.py:91-92). New private helper tertiary_actual_offset does the bounded 32-byte read via local_offset (no unwrap/panic, R-CODE-2). Then flip the two divergence_tertiary tests from #[ignore] to #[test] and update the stale directory.rs:559 'not followed' doc note + REQ-9 row.","created_at":"2026-07-11T21:57:44.650107926Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABArWfgTkBQYrjpPkyVJ0FMTD96ApAFZScPzgNSDc8O273psljfauRP5GOsZ+kWfJdXKUqoEGjJ5chMYFGUN/CuDA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEaye21Cf5dSivefaoSp40DCXc4zIrE6reCMOkpkUiYkSyNvjhmVCOmAuZVKizxtNPi2pgsyuDPbZskVoose5A8="}
{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":68,"timestamp":"2026-07-11T22:29:23.702839068Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"d691bf6c-5bf6-47f0-a0ca-d64fb76b0695","comment_uuid":"e1bec45d-0aae-4499-b850-b3fc80757758","author":"tLiK","content":"FIXED and verified. Commit 373f74bc extends walk_directories to follow tertiary (0x48/0x4A) L2 pointers via the Zen 4 double-indirection (32-byte block at entry offset; actual_offset = le_u32(block[16:20]); gen-id le_u32(block[20:24]); unknown gen only warns, still recurses) mirroring directory.py:85-99.\n\nVerification (nix dev shell, committed corpus):\n- crates/psptool-core: 146 lib + 54 + 3 tests, 0 failed\n- divergence_tertiary.rs: BOTH pins now PASS (0x48 known-gen + 0x4A unknown-gen), moved from #[ignore] to #[test]\n- corpus_roundtrip: 54 passed, 0 failed\n- differential (committed corpus): 49 passed, 0 failed, 5 pre-existing ignores\n- clippy -D warnings: clean; fmt: clean\n\nReal-corpus proof: the 3 ASRock AM5 images (B650/X870E/B850) no longer emit the \"directory sets differ / only the reference reports\" mismatch — they now surface all L2 directories. Their remaining differential failure is a SEPARATE address-mode divergence (tracked as #52), not this one. Closing.","created_at":"2026-07-11T22:29:23.698135362Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAy52v9KKYgvNVbfbmPIG4+HmejQ5o3LaYhB9OLWdccmhT0ezLGbYEZsXtRJNxN+XgG/ESnNw98fyrh5KOGf0KCw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHj6nj1Jxj8MEnMmdB8ycBnhkJgCkSVsd/9fXPd4INGUC+6+c+Mf33klPsDf/As2/cN4s8aP5z3VSvVklQ7//Q8="}
