{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":74,"timestamp":"2026-07-11T22:53:22.035727331Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ff3a9562-e292-4ffb-8f75-0c1d07d85917","comment_uuid":"91eb4ebc-7dc7-4cbb-9a6c-1d4c7df7ff6c","author":"tLiK","content":"Failing test at crates/psptool-core/tests/divergence_bios_compressed.rs::divergence_compressed_oversize_bios_entry_sized_from_zlib_header pins this. Currently returns ParseError::Truncated{what:\"entry body\", expected:5242912(=0x500020), available:4096}. Root cause: entry.rs::resolve_body treats the directory record size (uncompressed) as the on-flash body length and its body_end>blob_end guard fires, DROPPING the entry. Upstream file.py:293-311 re-sizes compressed entries from the zlib header (0x100 + le_u32@offset+0x14). Fix is in entry.rs (resolve_body), NOT address.rs — the resolved address 0x1e02000 already matches the reference exactly. Two controls in the same file prove the fixture is sound and that our bounds check is correct for the non-compressed case.","created_at":"2026-07-11T22:53:22.031126705Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAwASYaTc7Na6RG1JE4/miaGyVwaPPzqSKliZdXZOA6zS6J3UZ9irqTx9ZK75bF7INy5TR1gl1ng1OW5nR3fDJDg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAUes0MgiwcKZWeSYqh34nnXnd61Bgl8ncGkEFfdG3qD2Sl4jV4zm1EG1o3oT/o6c/buUIFmTpH/czsfM4N/bw0="}
{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":75,"timestamp":"2026-07-11T22:53:26.859829216Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"e5722ead-8cd4-4006-8598-6cb24d15adbd","comment_uuid":"4ae212fc-bb19-4f7f-8c9e-f18adffa62a7","author":"tLiK","content":"Oracle audit (PSPTOOL_REFERENCE vs live corpus) reclassifies both #52 symptoms — NEITHER is an address-mode bug:\n\nSYMPTOM B (AM5 BIOS, ASRock_B650): NOT address-mode. Reference and ours BOTH resolve $BL2@0x2ed000 e4 to address 0x1e02000 (identical). The divergence is body SIZE: record size=0x500020 is the UNCOMPRESSED size; the entry is compressed (flags bit3). Upstream sizes it from the zlib header to 0x8ab51 (fits); ours uses 0x500020 literally, overruns the 32MB ROM, returns Truncated, and DROPS e4/e5. Root cause: entry.rs::resolve_body. Filed as #59 with a failing pin.\n\nSYMPTOM A (EPYC upper-half, GENOAD8HM3 dir@0x1332000): NOT a code bug. Side-by-side vs reference shows EVERY entry address matches (idx0-10,12-15) EXCEPT idx11. Our idx11=0x13c8000 (type 0x1b) is the address-mode-CORRECT value (upper-ROM origin 0x1000000 + flash offset 0x3c8000 — exactly upstream's own arithmetic, proven by all sibling entries matching). Reference idx11=0x3c8000 (type 0x21 WRAPPED_IKEK) is upstream's files_by_offset cross-ROM CACHE ECHO (file.py:47-54): the rom-relative file_offset 0x3c8000 collides with dir@0x331000 in the lower ROM, and upstream reuses the first File. That is the documented equivalent-divergence #40, handled by the differential tolerance layer — not a production address bug. No test pinned for A (pinning ref's 0x3c8000 would assert upstream's cache quirk as the address contract).\n\naddress.rs arithmetic is correct; .design/psptool-core/address.md is NOT required for the fix.","created_at":"2026-07-11T22:53:26.855203663Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAW4GzQpTL6H4dp0bRrzgosG+dT5YZxwqmb2CqTv53R6mgEMw+dJXYLEXRC1wvBbS6iJ6Z+1ggTTUYEQI/3dDjCw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQH0KO86+xMzkJrYQ9TIcds76X0usGW4/TvYT6Ivpkcm80/0uLaAi8WT8Hu4IHv2dwWmBN+zHMkEsnxOeTPNGQAw="}
{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":76,"timestamp":"2026-07-11T22:58:37.267078805Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ff3a9562-e292-4ffb-8f75-0c1d07d85917","comment_uuid":"96921e0a-01e5-4a15-bf17-9c1c1d1ccd05","author":"tLiK","content":"Plan: resolve_body in crates/psptool-core/src/entry.rs currently returns ParseError::Truncated whenever body_end > blob_end, dropping compressed BIOS entries whose directory-record (uncompressed) size overruns the ROM. Fix mirrors upstream file.py:302-311 + utils.zlib_find_header (utils.py:218-234): thread the BIOS compressed flag (BiosEntry.is_compressed(), flags bit3) into resolve_body; when the record-size body overruns AND the entry is compressed, find the zlib header in blob[offset..] (checking 0x100 first) and size the on-flash body to zlib_hdr + le_u32(blob[offset+0x14..+0x18]) instead of erroring. Non-compressed oversize still returns Truncated (control test depends on it). Edits: add compressed param + zlib_find_header helper in entry.rs; parse_bios passes record.is_compressed(), parse_psp passes false. Then un-#[ignore] the pin test and flip design-doc REQ-6 to SHIPPED.","created_at":"2026-07-11T22:58:37.262565334Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAbknOliXjmky+5pG1XtrlcijJO06G50X/EX4W8hycpk/EPBxST5GhA+IHFV2CbCgYhuj3QE6LtGA5bhTT5FilDA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDseSVbcPmhqVebCFHnUcQp7AU/96gQlPTHSs/hce/ocF1DaZVBN7uZ3Ybzs8PesOkL9aCctwQ9xfnmqU1DuHQQ="}
