{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":134,"timestamp":"2026-07-12T04:06:30.422593138Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"5346afaa-652e-4838-a5c1-851082a0f96f","title":"psptool-ops: replace_entry_body is a vocabulary-only public export + stale-checksum footgun","description":"Current state: \n\nDesired state: \n\nReason: \n\nSurfaced by the replace.rs critic audit (post-#66). `replace_entry_body` (the entry-only path in crates/psptool-ops/src/replace.rs, re-exported at lib.rs:28) has NO non-test production consumer — the only production replace path (psptool-cli/src/cmds/replace.rs) uses `replace_psp_entry_body`/`replace_bios_entry_body`, which carry the parent directory and recompute the Fletcher-32 checksum (#66). `replace_entry_body` takes no parent handle, so it SKIPS the checksum recompute and emits a directory that fails its own verify_checksum — a footgun for any future caller.\n\nTwo goal.md concerns:\n- R-DEFER-1 (no vocabulary-only shipping): a public API surface with no production consumer.\n- Correctness footgun: silently produces stale-checksum output.\n\nOptions: (a) remove the public re-export / make it crate-private if genuinely unused; (b) require a parent-directory arg so it too recomputes the checksum (unifying with the family entry points); (c) keep it but return an explicit \"checksum-not-updated\" marker type so callers cannot accidentally emit stale directories. Recommend (a) unless a consumer is planned. Not a semantic divergence vs upstream (upstream always has a parent), so the critic correctly did not pin it — this is API hygiene.","priority":"low","parent_uuid":"525d7258-de71-4087-8d5a-f7dd155266b5","created_by":"tLiK"},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAgT/KnsckaNiWrBssjCrDSTlB+w2D+tjasDuSbjtDj6m25SaDhzAOZlijCLfDcitAglAyYy325MhDA74OV0AwM="