{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":139,"timestamp":"2026-07-12T04:24:33.824682364Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"52a1c711-a12a-42ae-b67e-82f906418fb2","title":"psptool-ops: replace.rs rewrite_size_field .expect can panic when zlib-recovered original_len exceeds u32 (R-CODE-2)","description":"Steps to reproduce:\n1. \n\nExpected: \nActual: \n\nSee HATER.md (committed) for the full adversarial analysis + failure scenario. Found by the-hater (Fable) review of the session's production changes. replace.rs:~234 .expect() assumes body.len() <= u32::MAX. The #59 zlib-recovery (entry.rs:~558, body_len = zlib_hdr(0x100)+zlib_size where zlib_size is le_u32) can yield original_len > u32::MAX; growth-rejection bounds new_body by original_len, so a crafted >=4GiB compressed entry + replacement panics instead of returning a typed Err. Fix: u32::try_from -> typed ReplaceError, no expect. Contrived trigger but a real panic-on-malformed-input path.","priority":"high","parent_uuid":"525d7258-de71-4087-8d5a-f7dd155266b5","created_by":"tLiK"},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNoqLjIXCSM8oJM/LOvk0jXbeFD2LI+0/5EiEeRGEiTzqtL5BIJz5JL3Jn1YOwREVwHdv6gnqfQKvBYMCuIHGAg="}
