{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":161,"timestamp":"2026-07-12T05:24:56.127438097Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"307dce04-e751-4448-9772-84e7a8cb63b2","comment_uuid":"f6336b5f-e6d4-41c7-a706-e3fd781249dd","author":"tLiK","content":"VERDICT: T1 CONFIRMED (live oracle + byte-level trace). The EPYC entry-11 divergence is upstream files_by_offset cross-ROM CACHE ECHO; OUR output is correct. NOT a code bug. Do NOT change the entry-body resolve path.\n\nEVIDENCE (GENOAD8HM3, reference = PSPTOOL_REFERENCE psptool 3.4, dual-ROM: ROM0 origin 0x0 mask 0x1ffffff / 32MiB; ROM1 origin 0x1000000 mask 0xffffff / 16MiB):\n\n1) RAW entry-11 record @ blob 0x1332000 (=ROM1 rom-rel 0x332000), bytes '1b0000000038000000803c0000000000':\n   type=0x1b size=0x3800 offset(loc)=0x3c8000 rsv0=0x0 (entry_addr_mode=0). Directory additional_info=0x20000750 -> directory address_mode=1 (FLASH-OFFSET).\n\n2) Upstream file_offset() (entry.py:61-63, addr_mode==1) returns self.offset RAW = 0x3c8000 -- a ROM-RELATIVE offset, NO mask, NO origin. Fresh absolute address = rom_origin(0x1000000)+0x3c8000 = 0x13c8000. That is EXACTLY our output AND upstream's own arithmetic.\n\n3) Reference 0x3c8000/type0x21/size0x30 comes SOLELY from the global files_by_offset cache (file.py:47-54, keyed by rom-relative file_offset). Key 0x3c8000 was seeded by ROM0 dir @0x331000 entry 9 (WRAPPED_IKEK type0x21 size0x30 get_address 0x3c8000), parsed before ROM1. Proven: the returned File.references == ['0x331000','0x1332000'] -- ONE File object shared across both ROMs.\n\n4) NO-COLLISION DISCRIMINATOR (killer): enumerated every entry of all 4 upper-ROM dirs (0x1062000 x53, 0x12f2000 x25, 0x1332000 x48, 0x1682000 x34). EXACTLY ONE cache echo exists: dir 0x1332000 idx11. Every other upper-ROM entry resolves origin+file_offset in BOTH tools (verified against our -E -j -r1: idx10=0x13b3f00, idx11=0x13c8000, idx12=0x13cb800). A systematic window/mask bug (T2) would hit ALL upper-ROM entries; it hits exactly the one collision.\n\nT2 DISPROVEN: entry rsv0=0 is irrelevant (directory mode=1 governs, not 2/3); addr_mode==1 does NO masking. The 0x13c8000 & 0xFFFFFF == 0x3c8000 coincidence is NOT a mask upstream applies -- it is the identity that the echoed ROM0 file sits at the same rom-relative offset (origin delta = 0x1000000). Upstream's file_offset() is rom-relative and never yields 0x3c8000 as an ABSOLUTE address for idx11 except via the cache.\n\nACTION: per R-CHAR-3 no failing test is pinned against our code (that would assert upstream's cache quirk as our contract). This is an equivalent divergence needing a DIFFERENTIAL-TOLERANCE rule (spec in next comment). The EPYC images are .local-corpus only; the 3 committed multi-ROM images stay SKIP_LISTed because #41 idx3 (type 0x64 vs 0x70) is a SEPARATE genuine mis-location the tolerance rule (condition 3 below) will NOT mask.","created_at":"2026-07-12T05:24:56.122790425Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAEiRRx3x/eG/jHoeQHVcY3JUUESFVL4XbeeiDf4X5lLgI3TTmWQc+BabJpNkdbOYyIf/2pvjQ0r42yyFyX/+3Bg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHjMQ0zzqrKhkAIZUb7ojobRBINIXgE6eD1lH3Q3i4nMdbMzPpv2/ciP2GKcU/aXzvPcJtTGnkJTWXVwSLeAqg8="}
{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":162,"timestamp":"2026-07-12T05:25:18.234347045Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"307dce04-e751-4448-9772-84e7a8cb63b2","comment_uuid":"cf02b5a7-d544-4f7d-9c6d-2d231c356b85","author":"tLiK","content":"DIFFERENTIAL-TOLERANCE RULE SPEC (for a fixer/builder to implement; NOT implemented here).\n\nLOCATION: crates/psptool-cli/tests/differential.rs, fn compare_structure (lines 411-493), inside the per-entry loop at lines 460-490 -- add a guard BEFORE the entry_diff call at line 469 (alongside the existing consecutive-echo guard at 466). Also extend the module-doc 'Entries sharing a flash offset' note (lines 40-51) to cover the CROSS-ROM case.\n\nMECHANISM CITE: file.py:47-54 (create_file_if_not_exists reuses files_by_offset[entry.file_offset()]); entry.py:38-63 (file_offset() is ROM-RELATIVE); blob.py:32 (_MAX_PAGE_SIZE = 16 MiB window); rom.py addr_mask = rom_size-1. The cache key is the 16-MiB-window rom-relative offset and the dict is GLOBAL across ROMs, so an upper-ROM entry whose rom-relative offset collides with an earlier (lower-ROM) file echoes that lower file.\n\nRULE: treat entry N as a cross-ROM cache echo (skip its address/size/sectionType comparison) iff ALL hold:\n  (1) oe.address != re.address; AND\n  (2) re.address == oe.address & 0x00FF_FFFF  AND  re.address < oe.address\n      (equivalently: oe.address - re.address is a nonzero multiple of 0x0100_0000 and shares the 16-MiB-window offset) -- our value is the fresh upper-ROM absolute address, reference is the page-0 rom-relative echo; AND\n  (3) the reference's own projection ('theirs') contains, in SOME OTHER directory, an entry with address==re.address && size==re.size && sectionType==re.sectionType -- i.e. upstream's reported value is literally a real file living at that lower address elsewhere (the cache SEED).\n\nCondition (3) is the safety discriminator: a genuine mis-parse (e.g. #41 idx3 type0x64-vs-0x70) will NOT have upstream's reported triple existing as a real file elsewhere, so it is NOT masked -- those images correctly stay failing/SKIP_LISTed until their real bug is fixed. This rule tolerates ONLY true echoes.\n\nSCOPE: with this rule, GENOAD8HM3 and TURIND12M3 differential passes clean (single echo idx11 tolerated). It does NOT by itself clear the 3 committed multi-ROM SKIP_LIST images -- those have additional genuine divergences (#41 idx3).","created_at":"2026-07-12T05:25:18.229795866Z","kind":"decision","signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAkrBGft9H6CBNJwItA2soEKno4TDRJm6sYFeaFErASyJDFh6TYO54l/rLJKvb0oKt3kkpy46qZCAWNep3+025Dw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLrAyybwyAMZc3BRYE3ozjuIURrYZBVioOgnUsL5whRArctKcFKonc8ORqc0ThddLZ7V2/conJniTtoSTVE7lgQ="}
