{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":165,"timestamp":"2026-07-12T05:28:22.193561224Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"307dce04-e751-4448-9772-84e7a8cb63b2","comment_uuid":"9b9040b4-85f6-494e-9889-2d9b60ee79ed","author":"tLiK","content":"Plan (acto-fixer, #41 T1 tolerance): edit crates/psptool-cli/tests/differential.rs (test harness, no translate-gate). (1) Extend the module-doc 'Entries sharing a flash offset' note (~40-51) with accommodation (c): cross-ROM files_by_offset cache echo, citing file.py:47-54 (create_file_if_not_exists reuses files_by_offset[file_offset()]), entry.py:38-63 (file_offset is rom-relative), blob.py:32 (16 MiB window). (2) Add a guard in compare_structure before the entry_diff call (~469), alongside the consecutive-echo guard (~466): skip entry N's address/size/sectionType comparison iff ALL of (a) oe.address != re.address, (b) re.address == oe.address & 0x00FF_FFFF AND re.address < oe.address, (c) safety discriminator: theirs contains in SOME OTHER directory an entry with address==re.address && size==re.size && sectionType==re.section_type (cache seed). Reasoning: upstream file_offset() is rom-relative (addr_mode==1 returns raw offset); the global files_by_offset dict echoes a lower-ROM file when an upper-ROM rom-relative offset collides. Our upper-ROM absolute is correct (T1 verdict). Condition (c) leaves genuine mis-parses (#41 idx3 type 0x64 vs 0x70, no seed) failing.","created_at":"2026-07-12T05:28:22.189030393Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA8WDtgdTgjeCJ9Ef0pOcg5AnKjNRE9yq7zEwJjykr+1mJWPRpfVo4bfkPfJi7fqMjApVCMVO36IZkOwMty0DFBQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3Nsa