{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":166,"timestamp":"2026-07-12T05:37:04.848916316Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"307dce04-e751-4448-9772-84e7a8cb63b2","comment_uuid":"575b7eb6-7fce-4dc7-9e1e-00948180b914","author":"tLiK","content":"Result (acto-fixer): #41 T1 differential-tolerance rule implemented in crates/psptool-cli/tests/differential.rs (commit 4e5d9d8d95e8). Cross-ROM files_by_offset cache-echo guard added to compare_structure with the 3-condition rule as specified (incl. the cache-seed safety discriminator).\n\nFINDING that supersedes the pre-trace hypothesis: ALL THREE committed multi-ROM blobs now pass the REAL differential comparison and were removed from SKIP_LIST (R-DEFER-3). The earlier reconciliation predicted #41 idx3 (H12SSW9 dir@0x1246000, ours PMU_CODE~0x64 @0x1249000 size 0x4990 vs reference BIOS_L2_PTR~0x70 @0x249000 size 0x400) was a GENUINE mis-location with no seed. Byte-level verification against the live oracle proves otherwise:\n  - The reference triple (0x249000 / 0x400 / type-0x70) has a REAL cache seed at ROM-0 dir @0x117000 idx13 (identical BIOS_L2_PTR~0x70 file). Condition (3) matches a bona-fide seed, not a spurious one.\n  - Upstream -E -j emits the CACHED File's type, not the directory-entry type — exactly as the T1 trace already proved for EPYC entry-11 (reference type 0x21 vs raw entry type 0x1b). So idx3's 0x64-vs-0x70 type difference is the identical echo signature, NOT a mis-parse.\nTherefore idx3 is a true cross-ROM cache echo; OUR output (fresh ROM-1 record) is correct. There is no remaining genuine mis-parse in #41.\n\nVERIFICATION (nix dev shell): committed differential 53 passed / 0 failed / 1 ignored (only AORUS #60, unrelated); clippy + fmt clean; local .local-corpus 2 EPYC (GENOAD8HM3, TURIND12M3) pass, 3 AM5 fail only on #60 (version-skew type-0x5c WMOS), unrelated. Every #41 pin is green -> closing.","created_at":"2026-07-12T05:37:04.844246008Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegT