{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":168,"timestamp":"2026-07-12T05:45:33.734337293Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"ca74b297-d703-4ae4-b2b2-0769a8ebc969","title":"harden #41 cross-ROM echo tolerance: condition (3) value-match could theoretically mask a coincidental-duplicate mis-parse","description":"Current state: \n\nDesired state: \n\nReason: \n\nNon-manifesting hardening note from the #41 tolerance verification (differential.rs cross_rom_echo guard, ~477-507). Condition (3) matches the cache seed by (address,size,sectionType) VALUE-equality in some other directory. The TRUE mechanism is upstream files_by_offset OBJECT identity (File.references links the seed dir to the echoing dir) + the exact 0x1000000-window-multiple address relationship. In theory a genuine over-add mis-parse whose coincidental page-0 triple happens to duplicate elsewhere could be tolerated. Verified NOT to manifest on the current corpus (all 7 tolerated entries are object-identity echoes; no untolerated failures; no coincidental masking). Optional hardening: tighten condition (3) to also require the seed be in a LOWER ROM (re.address < 16MiB window boundary / owner in ROM0) and/or that oe.address-re.address be exactly rom_origin, reducing coincidence surface. Low priority — defensive only.","priority":"low","parent_uuid":"525d7258-de71-4087-8d5a-f7dd155266b5","created_by":"tLiK"},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKu53YJ+sARwxLQlBlE+n7iDjSquPmVi2hwIzLTxHhTJY8WebsaOAnwZxrfHhMRjup2YB17uA2Nd30f7e+Wh0ww="}
