{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":170,"timestamp":"2026-07-12T05:50:10.705223613Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"52a1c711-a12a-42ae-b67e-82f906418fb2","comment_uuid":"e2e9bbe1-a52f-4fe5-a81e-7f86c173bbff","author":"tLiK","content":"Plan: replace.rs rewrite_size_field (~234, ~239). (1) u32::try_from(new_size).expect(...) -> .map_err(|_| ReplaceError::SizeTooLarge { size: new_size })?. (2) record.offset().checked_add(4).expect(...) -> .ok_or(ReplaceError::RecordOffsetOverflow)?. Add two typed enum variants. Reasoning: entry.py:108-110 size setter packs a 4-byte u32 (struct.pack('<I', value)); a new_size > u32::MAX cannot be represented in the on-disk 4-byte size field, so it is a malformed/untrusted-input path that must return a typed Err per goal.md R-CODE-2, not panic. Trigger is a >=4GiB zlib-recovered entry slot (entry.rs zlib-recovery) that lifts original_len (and thus the growth-bounded new_size) past u32::MAX. Add a #[cfg(test)] value-level test passing new_size=0x1_0000_0000 directly (no allocation).","created_at":"2026-07-12T05:50:10.700423610Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA/Z2StxUiPpGsKHHTyum6wcGJot02brUJoNsAayrsp9IpXcUChcc56uqj5r2PV5zab8hIWN7Ik6g6M6uWswABBQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQORpVVF7zkp8eUyfl1YmQocbgO+1+o8hP+yypikkbukSNgZdybhkibEt79we4wivcRI5vd8y3QZhnSrhEuiorAw="}
