{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":176,"timestamp":"2026-07-12T06:37:38.314339531Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ab6eb2e6-0890-4a93-8d75-8954a4c84d61","comment_uuid":"a6143c15-c82a-4937-b455-001318bb1afb","author":"tLiK","content":"RESOLVED (byte-order confirmed WRONG) + NEW divergence found. Live oracle run of reference PSPTool over vendor/test-corpus proves the real-firmware HeaderFile convention: a signed HeaderFile verifies ONLY with (a) signed region = 0x100 + size_signed bytes AND (b) PLAIN, NON-reversed on-disk signature. Every other combination (reversed, or total==size_signed) verifies False. So BOTH target choices are wrong vs real firmware:\n\n- Divergence B (REQ-8, this issue): body.rs:392-393 sig_be.reverse() and sign.rs:174-175 sig_disk.reverse() must be DROPPED for HeaderFiles (upstream cert_tree.py:63 uses plain Signature, crypto.py:247 verifies non-reversed).\n- Divergence A (NEW, falsifies REQ-1 'SHIPPED'): HeaderEntry::get_signed_bytes (body.rs:333-349) truncates the TOTAL to size_signed; upstream truncates to len(header)+size_signed = 0x100+size_signed (header_file.py:162-164). Off by 0x100 bytes.\n\nEvidence: verify_chain_of_trust over the corpus reports 0 Verified / 2843 BadSignature. Failing pin committed at crates/psptool-ops/tests/divergence_signature_byte_order.rs::real_corpus_headerfile_verifies_under_verify_chain_of_trust (#[ignore], tracking #78). Passing oracle control real_corpus_headerfile_convention_is_nonreversed_and_full_length isolates both axes A and B against the on-disk bytes.","created_at":"2026-07-12T06:37:38.309745159Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA3JVf5gGRsDrvXiDs4be9GdcUcVzp6YSsmYAhXlhZ/ZuUa5XhHPcHUZ6LInRFBwRLwgMnytMpZ91Oa2xeil3gBA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQ