{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":207,"timestamp":"2026-07-12T08:45:46.244990490Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"baf95e0a-6573-4d87-9496-8706ff0a6371","title":"Divergence: HeaderEntry::signature_bytes (body.rs:222) ignores is_signed — returns last signature_len bytes for an unsigned HeaderFile","description":"Spillover of #81 into the sibling method. header_file.py:77-84 sets signature_len=0 for an unsigned file (never materializes self.signature); the observable signature is empty (to_decrypted_file_bytes header_file.py:181: b'' when not is_signed). body.rs:227 calls signature_len() UNCONDITIONALLY (no is_signed gate), so for an unsigned file (signed_raw==0, signature_type==0) it returns body[end-0x100..end] instead of empty. This also contradicts the #81 data_region fix (body.rs:200) which now gates sig_len on is_signed, so for the same unsigned entry data_region and signature_bytes OVERLAP on the last 0x100 bytes. Not currently production-reachable (sign.rs:123 and verify.rs:256 both gate on is_signed before the call; extract.rs calls only data_region), but signature_bytes is a pub library API. Failing pin: crates/psptool-core/tests/divergence_body_bounds.rs::signature_bytes_of_unsigned_headerfile_is_empty.","priority":"medium","created_by":"tLiK"},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPUMUpk/r0cRnWWNim2zqsG0VpneJI9GF5pcN2xAd458tqncVAS1Hx5yhg0mxrDyscAfpb2uDYKUQb/p3OfY8gw="}
