{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":241,"timestamp":"2026-07-12T09:42:26.230810779Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"99e1710e-053d-417e-802e-e1c86fb8cb62","comment_uuid":"bf09ff92-6407-49dd-92f4-e4bfbdfc1204","author":"tLiK","content":"Gap: upstream '-X -u' single/multi returns file.get_signed_bytes() (__main__.py:172,194) = header(0x100) ++ get_decrypted_decompressed_body()[:0x100+size_signed] (header_file.py:162-164) — decrypt-THEN-decompress, header-prefixed, truncated to size_signed. Rust extract_decompressed (extract.rs:57-62) returns only zlib_inflate(data_region) via get_decompressed_body (body.rs:304): NO header prefix, NO size_signed truncation, NO decrypt-first for encrypted+compressed entries. Likewise upstream '-X -c' SINGLE returns file.to_decrypted_file_bytes() (__main__.py:176) = header(enc-flags cleared) ++ get_decrypted_body() ++ signature (header_file.py:176-182); Rust extract_decrypted (extract.rs:77-81) returns only get_decrypted_body() (body.rs:267). Core get_signed_bytes already exists (body.rs:377, used by sign.rs) — the gap is the extract path uses the wrong primitive. Not caught by any suite (parity_ops=[]; extract not in ls/ls_json differential). Fix during extract.rs read->write->verify pass.","created_at":"2026-07-12T09:42:26.225913390Z","kind":"note","signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA1UqmvTXSL3OHbkqRt8iLsBRZW070DC8fA9AGGqlNEDKMWvuKqJYwPQuCaKSCrNyQnbboaFs6FEbexHU0mgdCCQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFyLa5PY867VfcwX6D47XRURxd6HsDfs2oxIhWrB6yC1e/WONdHRZAXo/lG2mmHuTh/hqlOx9x5Ft6X2CblWeQY="}
{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":242,"timestamp":"2026-07-12T09:53:17.353609718Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"99e1710e-053d-417e-802e-e1c86fb8cb62","comment_uuid":"14574d43-97af-4274-88d9-8d4276d23edb","author":"tLiK","content":"Failing tests pinning the #88 divergence landed at crates/psptool-ops/tests/divergence_extract_envelope.rs:\n\n- divergence_decompress_envelope_matches_get_signed_bytes (single-file -X -u): asserts extract_decompressed == upstream get_signed_bytes() = header(0x100) ++ decrypted-decompressed-body[..0x100+size_signed] (__main__.py:172, header_file.py:162-164). FAILS under --ignored: target returns bare 17-byte inflated body, expected header-prefixed + size_signed-truncated envelope.\n- divergence_decrypt_envelope_matches_to_decrypted_file_bytes (single-file -X -c): asserts extract_decrypted == upstream to_decrypted_file_bytes() = header(is_encrypted+IV cleared) ++ decrypted-body ++ signature (__main__.py:176, header_file.py:176-182). FAILS under --ignored: target returns bare decrypted body only.\n\nBoth #[ignore]d with tracking #88; run 'cargo test -p psptool-ops --test divergence_extract_envelope -- --ignored' to observe the pinned failures. Fixer must target the SINGLE-file contract (-u -> get_signed_bytes, -c -> to_decrypted_file_bytes); note upstream's own single-vs-multi -c inconsistency (multi uses get_decrypted_body(), __main__.py:195-196,218-219).","created_at":"2026-07-12T09:53:17.348894924Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA5pu/Aq86LzqkEFoJE2j9bPuBDId3JW9wgsZV0k6MBccGl9D/xhczp5qGB/OTVkTybRIxhrbIzuAIKkUNfpTaBQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5r