{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":245,"timestamp":"2026-07-12T10:05:31.037757885Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"99e1710e-053d-417e-802e-e1c86fb8cb62","comment_uuid":"4a6dfe1a-fd77-417a-be9c-fa5079b404ca","author":"tLiK","content":"Result (fixer): REVERTED — fix scope exceeds single-file/dispatch model; needs orchestrator re-dispatch (likely acto-builder).\n\nThe specified compose (extract_decompressed -> get_signed_bytes; extract_decrypted -> to_decrypted_file_bytes inline) DOES make BOTH pinned tests PASS under --ignored. But it breaks 5 pre-existing in-file unit tests in extract.rs, and 2 of those cannot be made green within extract.rs alone:\n\n1. SignedRegionOutOfRange(281,17): the committed header_compressed fixture stamps size_signed=281 (header-INCLUSIVE, stale pre-#79 convention, build_fixtures.rs:362) while get_signed_bytes treats size_signed as header-EXCLUSIVE; decompressed body is only 17 bytes. Requires regenerating the .bin in crate psptool-fixtures (another file) OR rewriting the unit test to synthesize a body.\n\n2. NotCompressed gate lost (REQ-2/REQ-4): get_signed_bytes tolerates non-compressed input; upstream keeps the 'not compressed' guard in the CLI (__main__.py:170), NOT in get_signed_bytes. extract_decompressed_errors_when_header_not_compressed and _works_on_keystore_class assert NotCompressed. Preserving that end-to-end needs the gate moved into cmds/extract.rs (CLI, forbidden by dispatch).\n\n3/4. extract_decrypted round-trip + wrong-ikek tests assert the BARE plaintext; trivially updatable to the envelope (in-file), but bundled with 1/2 above.\n\nPer R-FIX-3/R-FIX-6 the working tree was reverted to HEAD (baseline green: cargo test -p psptool-ops --lib extract = 14 passed). #80 helper hygiene fix (size_signed header-exclusive) is independent and correct but reverted alongside since dispatch bundled it.\n\nRecommendation: re-dispatch as acto-builder with a manifest covering extract.rs + cmds/extract.rs (NotCompressed/NotEncrypted single-file guards) + psptool-fixtures header_compressed regeneration + the in-file test rewrites + REQ-2/3/7 table. The KeyStore multi-file nuance stays separate as noted.","created_at":"2026-07-12T10:05:31.032991814Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAWZxiOIxPH/262RQ1ZJwiQBvFSbC85rO28OVwnmycQD7TwNabo8dXRzFpbfunBaiyNmKcz6ztmWssi7m76rmVBA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMThdCCe1YI3FivaphdC4DAQXwFwAOdwr+2FcO+DV5Ktmwzsi6wxyLQEbLJQmRqXKw9ZFwpXwAIZvauO2sdeOwA="}
{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":246,"timestamp":"2026-07-12T10:31:07.734546321Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"0b2e6ea5-c7c5-43f0-b554-8f8f23477ccf","comment_uuid":"abe75a8d-012c-4a55-99f3-c9cb4ac5356b","author":"tLiK","content":"Failing pin at crates/psptool-core/tests/divergence_zlib_rom_window.rs:divergence_rom_window_smaller_than_blob demonstrates the divergence. Two-ROM fixture (16 MiB blob, 8 MiB rom_size): a compressed $BL2 entry at ROM-relative 0x7FF000 with uncompressed size 0x500020 overruns the 8 MiB ROM window but NOT the 16 MiB whole file. Upstream (file.py:297) bounds the overrun by parent_buffer.buffer_size (ROM window) -> zlib recovery -> body len 0x140 (zlib_hdr 0x100 + zlib_size 0x40, file.py:303-311). Our resolve_body bounds by whole-file blob_end (entry.rs:537, blob_end=blob_start+blob.len() at entry.rs:517) -> normal path -> returns raw uncompressed 0x500020 bytes spilling into ROM#1. rom_size/rom_origin (params entry.rs:500-501) carry the correct bound rom_origin+rom_size but are unused at the :537 check. Test FAILS under --ignored: left=5242912 (0x500020), right=320 (0x140). Fix = bound overrun by rom_origin+rom_size clamped to blob_end. #[ignore]d tracking #72.","created_at":"2026-07-12T10:31:07.729797553Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAZRDDjeWzTC/sUnBzrDvl6nA34HizqfKJ96KraVko3NcgCI6g06AcYpq4UlT7mRmpXzCWSarogc7dJXhleB/MAA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKEqrAxq2Ukr9rikPaQsdpKd9vQPtfj9Y/SwPyb78bMXeywmgVts9KBg4XmVpOTygTZHnSudkWuWrHmFShuwjQs="}
{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":247,"timestamp":"2026-07-12T10:33:21.002054614Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"0b2e6ea5-c7c5-43f0-b554-8f8f23477ccf","comment_uuid":"42505a4b-a3ab-41d0-b560-a83056f0e963","author":"tLiK","content":"Plan (acto-fixer): entry.rs resolve_body overrun trigger.\n\nEdit ONLY crates/psptool-core/src/entry.rs.\n\n- entry.rs:537 currently triggers zlib-recovery on `body_end > blob_end` where blob_end (entry.rs:517) is the WHOLE-FILE end. Upstream file.py:297 bounds the overrun by the ROM WINDOW (`parent_buffer.buffer_size >= entry.file_offset() + entry.size`), not the whole file.\n- Coordinate space: body_offset/body_end/blob_start/blob_end are absolute (whole-file). rom_origin.get() is the ROM's absolute start, rom_size.bytes() its length, so rom_origin.get()+rom_size.bytes() is the ROM window's absolute end — directly comparable to the absolute body_end.\n- Fix: introduce `rom_window_end = min(rom_origin.get()+rom_size.bytes(), blob_end)` (saturating_add; clamped to blob_end so a ROM window past the actual input never reads OOB) and change the :537 trigger to `body_end > rom_window_end`. blob_end retained for the error 'available' field and final slice fallback.\n- Single-ROM: rom_origin+rom_size == blob_end, so the bound is unchanged (no regression). Multi-ROM: an entry overrunning its 8 MiB ROM window (but not the 16 MiB file) now recovers to zlib_hdr+zlib_size=0x140, matching upstream.\n\nWHY upstream behaves this way: file.py comment 293-296 — components not on 16MB boundary use entry.offset to detect overflow of the PARENT (ROM) buffer; a compressed entry overrunning the ROM window is zlib-recovered, not sized to its raw uncompressed record size.","created_at":"2026-07-12T10:33:20.995391194Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAgAS1dusze40onPMHRSImzS59aTIMuPcTKjwolbuaXKi+b2cC7yzeAdKCBYdIWPIaZecWk0brUAoF97xtmvTHAw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIn9QfBUqvRpEikKRKY0HtdjxH+ZMbSiVBn4DUVUt8rZEiqM4uNIKAPPWhUjqq6TxKaS0w/tcTi3g6LwSIk7UwQ="}
{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":248,"timestamp":"2026-07-12T10:35:18.385671322Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"0b2e6ea5-c7c5-43f0-b554-8f8f23477ccf","comment_uuid":"41b63204-1a96-4eb6-8c04-b0ce6322d4fe","author":"tLiK","content":"Fix applied and verified (NOT committed — left in working tree for orchestrator to seal; #[ignore] left in place per dispatch).\n\nentry.rs resolve_body: overrun trigger now bounds by the ROM window instead of whole-file blob_end. Added `rom_window_end = min(rom_origin.get()+rom_size.bytes(), blob_end)` (saturating) and changed the :537 trigger from `body_end > blob_end` to `body_end > rom_window_end`. +15 -1, single file.\n\nGauntlet (nix-shell default.nix -A shell):\n- divergence_zlib_rom_window --include-ignored: 2 passed, 0 failed (pin divergence_rom_window_smaller_than_blob PASS; control_rom_window_equals_blob_recovers green).\n- cargo test -p psptool-core: 146 passed, 0 failed (+ all bin targets 0 failed; divergence bin shows 1 ignored = the still-#[ignore]d pin per dispatch).\n- corpus_roundtrip: 54 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored, 0 skipped.\n- differential: 53 passed, 0 failed, 1 ignored (pre-existing unrelated), 0 skipped.\n- clippy --all-targets -D warnings: PASS.\n- cargo fmt --check: PASS.\n\nSingle-ROM images unaffected (rom_origin+rom_size == blob_end there). No regression.","created_at":"2026-07-12T10:35:18.380733425Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAP0lwhxsygceLXyVPg0bSdpkeotMEegH7uyC8rDwJjXvyTlsRjaOx6hZRW9a0/6LMNFMJCQPYqF/reZPkiUqcAg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQH0jOmnniaGtgfusxIUV