{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":265,"timestamp":"2026-10-18T22:42:36.745527215Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"f7dd168c-f826-4ad4-adec-395534c077bf","title":"Divergence: zero-size directory record classified Plain, upstream parses it as a HeaderFile (header_file.py:32-33) and echoes it for the next same-offset record","description":"Spillover from #89. Upstream HeaderFile._parse grows buffer_size to 0x100 for entries with size 0 ('give those with a entry size of 0 a chance to get their header parsed', header_file.py:32-33), so a zero-size record pointing at a real header becomes a HeaderFile; the next directory record at the same offset is then the files_by_offset echo of it (file.py:47-50). Rust entry.rs classify() sees a 0-byte body and yields EntryClass::Plain, and parses the following record fresh. Corpus impact (vs upstream 241629b decode tally): ASUS_Notebook_TUF_FX505DY-AS.309 dir1 idx17/18 @0x1e9000 (KVM_IMAGE size 0 then S0I3_DRIVER), Lenovo_Thinkpad_A285 @0x3bf220 and A485 @0x51f420 idx14/15 (KVM_IMAGE size 0 then ABL0): upstream counts 2 HeaderFiles at each offset, we count 1. Pinned as named deltas in crates/psptool-ops/tests/decode_verification.rs ENTRY_SET_DELTA; fixing this must update that constant.","priority":"high","parent_uuid":"525d7258-de71-4087-8d5a-f7dd155266b5","created_by":"tLiK"},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOkfWDNB/RM0opa1jnbJp+vVMvaKg/0ezdouItq6VFp3ZLA1Pr5u1F14iP5BS22wf1MJlnTcOi/50KIa3i098Qc="}
