{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":267,"timestamp":"2026-10-18T22:42:56.444970501Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e08438bf-e7a4-4f28-8ab7-4367b77fb377","title":"Divergence: body.rs find_zlib_start (extract path) takes the earliest of any zlib magic, upstream zlib_find_header tries magics in priority order (utils.py:224-232); get_decompressed_body accepts truncated zlib streams","description":"Spillover from #89. utils.py:224-232 iterates ZLIB_TYPES in order (78DA, 789C, 785E, 7801): for each magic it checks s[0x100:0x102] then s.find(magic), returning the first magic found ANYWHERE before trying the next magic. body.rs find_zlib_start (used by get_decompressed_body -> extract -c / get_signed_bytes) returns the earliest offset of ANY magic, so '78 9C' at 0x10 beats '78 DA' at 0x200 where upstream picks 0x200. entry.rs zlib_find_header is the faithful port; the #89 decode ladder (body.rs decode_best_effort) uses it. Second gap on the same path: get_decompressed_body inflates via flate2 Read, which returns the partial output of a TRUNCATED stream as success, whereas zlib.decompress raises (utils.py:250). body.rs zlib_decompress_strict (#89) is the faithful inflate. No corpus image currently exercises either difference.","priority":"medium","parent_uuid":"525d7258-de71-4087-8d5a-f7dd155266b5","created_by":"tLiK"},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKr6O6tPMVZzSiwzwZzrldnY7HWpg0lPpGe26Xml9dxzj7rj9wa5rCJ1DSEL4IMKIMB3N+fzZ8Z5U7dlUGHZlAc="}
