{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":294,"timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:36:57.389033512Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"f68dfb32-8ad2-4064-9530-a2e786b1a249","comment_uuid":"2ff55b67-7d6e-44ac-9e69-c45a6c62a8bf","author":"tLiK","content":"Plan: Reproduced (release ext, py3.13, corpus test_files): RSS +32 MB/ROM parse-only, +40-48 MB/ROM with get_decrypted_decompressed_body, gc.collect() has no effect. Root cause by measurement: no psptool._native type has Py_TPFLAGS_HAVE_GC (gc.is_tracked(psp)==False for PSPTool/Blob/Rom/File; __flags__ bit 14 clear), so the upstream-mandated cycles (psptool.blob<->blob.psptool, rom.fet<->fet.rom, dir.entries[i].parent_directory<->dir, dir.header.parent_buffer<->dir) run through instance __dict__s the collector cannot traverse; every ROM's graph + its Arc<Image> (image + snapshot copy = 2x ROM size) is retained forever. Probe: manually clearing every graph object's __dict__ before del -> RSS flat at 44 MB over 6 ROMs, so no Rust-side Arc cycle / static cache is involved. The dict-traversal gap is pyo3 0.25 itself (fixed upstream in 0.29.1, PyO3#6206; also PyO3#6198/#6234: 0.25 never decrefs a pyclass(dict) instance's __dict__ on dealloc). Weak parent refs rejected: upstream attributes are strong both ways, so holding only a File (or PSPTool.from_file(p).blob) keeps the graph alive upstream; weak upward links would change that. Fix: (1) pyo3 0.25 -> 0.29.3 in psptool-py (mechanical API migration; Cargo.lock moves, reported as manifest expansion), so every pyclass(dict) is a GC type whose tp_traverse/tp_clear visit/clear __dict__; (2) NestedBuffer __traverse__/__clear__ for the Rust-held parent link; (3) weakref support on the graph classes (upstream objects are weakref-able) for collectability tests. Tests: test_api.py weakref collectability + is_tracked + synthetic RSS-bound over N parses of the 8 MiB image; corpus-gated RSS test (tests/memory.rs). Gauntlet + corpus_parity 108/108.","created_at":"2026-10-19T02:36:57.361706992Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA82hbaB3dco5zGJAvbKXFgldqJ6uK82Eeq7iPfxqDFToeUDK9Xjzq28BT0xfFfBHyYcPaYvg9DNWdmHVaSYJOBw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDrl7A7FoKk9Odlb12BD9VyODvhNRMCLZy2eNbcLDTQs6NP6gb6nyGYzjkXzHd6xXbnJLNpZntx5CAQlJzvE2gs="}
{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":295,"timestamp":"2026-10-19T03:07:02.719946283Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"f68dfb32-8ad2-4064-9530-a2e786b1a249","comment_uuid":"4067fa64-887f-47d8-9d89-42ee9b5b797f","author":"tLiK","content":"Result: commit 3df62fe8 (on 11670c64). Root cause: pyo3 0.25 pyclass(dict) types were not GC types, so upstream's attribute cycles (through __dict__ and the Rust-held NestedBuffer.parent) were invisible to the collector; no parse was ever freed. Fix: pyo3 0.29.3 (dict traversal, PyO3#6206), NestedBuffer __traverse__/__clear__, weakref on graph classes, memory.rs native-bytes trigger (gc.collect() at PSPTool construction once registered image/snapshot/decode-cache bytes cross max(128 MiB, 2x survivors); DEVIATIONS.md 21). RSS, 216 corpus parses + decode + drop, no explicit collect, py3.13 release: before +32-48 MB/ROM unbounded; GC-only 1.33 GB plateau/1.70 GB peak; fixed 384 MB peak (upstream 241629b: 672 MB peak). 54-ROM probe: before +2270 MiB, fixed +320 MiB. Tests: test_api.py TestMemory (5; 4 fail pre-fix, trigger test fails with trigger off), tests/memory.rs corpus probe (<512 MiB growth). Gauntlet: fmt, clippy -D warnings, cargo test --workspace (corpus_parity 108/108, corpus_roundtrip 54/54, differential 54/54), nix-build -A python (23 tests OK, imports OK). Manifest expansion: Cargo.lock (pyo3 bump). Env note: dev shell PSPTOOL_REFERENCE predating the 241629b repin is stale (no decode_verification) and fails subclass_parity independently; re-enter nix-shell.","created_at":"2026-10-19T03:07:02.695214607Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAVFNCckI2Msptj6BMQw95wl4fMIK5PC4y+z/KgwPk4LAjPLlT9vaxUWjksYzRrC5Qfy4Q8XqTnkf9d5692fUVDA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signat