{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":298,"timestamp":"2026-10-19T10:25:43.805899940Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"50491d93-029c-44a2-8f99-1f6ad1397c7d","title":"Divergence: extract -u/-c read a HeaderFile from the directory-sized entry body; upstream grows the buffer to rom_size (header_file.py:72-75)","description":"Spillover from #91. HeaderFile._parse grows buffer_size to rom_size when rom_size exceeds the directory-declared size (header_file.py:74-75 'elif self.rom_size > self.buffer_size: self.buffer_size = self.rom_size'), reading on into the parent buffer. psptool-ops extract_decompressed/extract_decrypted hand HeaderEntry the directory-sized entry.body, so effective_end rejects rom_size > body.len() as BodyTooSmall. Corpus: 13 compressed HeaderFiles (e.g. ASUS_PRIME-X470-PRO-ASUS-4804.CAP @0x2ee000, Acer_R01-A4.CAP @0x284000) where upstream -X -u returns bytes and ours errors 'body too small (147456 bytes) for header + signature (193548 bytes)'. The decode ladder already reads the grown window (body.rs Entry::header_file_window, private); extract needs the blob (or a pub window accessor) to do the same. Pinned by crates/psptool-cli/tests/extract_oracle.rs corpus_grown_headerfile_window_matches_reference (#[ignore]).","priority":"medium","parent_uuid":"525d7258-de71-4087-8d5a-f7dd155266b5","created_by":"tLiK"},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQB/izEx0k0pdF25v6+q05MOjvQkjEAn0s/DqmBGx3sFEIcBb1UgcGP7021V5X8ZgFNskiFWsxKW+WbfQzDvbwAE="}
