{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":326,"timestamp":"2026-10-19T20:44:30.431854028Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"da718d13-3f0f-4f02-ba1f-f5f9b99d0ee9","comment_uuid":"7df8369f-38a6-4539-88a5-9908b27c52f3","author":"tLiK","content":"Spillover from #90. Upstream SignedEntity.resign_only (cert_tree.py:101-117) signs self.file.get_signed_bytes() and writes the signature into the HeaderFile's signature NestedBuffer at rom_size - signature_len (header_file.py:88), i.e. over the buffer grown by header_file.py:32-33 / :72-75. psptool-ops/src/sign.rs sign_entry_with_rng uses entry.body (header.get_signed_bytes(body_bytes), header.signature_bytes(body_bytes)), so re-signing any HeaderFile whose buffer outgrows its directory size fails: the 13 corpus HeaderFiles grown past a non-zero directory size (#99, BodyTooSmall) and, since #90, the 3 zero-size KVM_IMAGE records (ASUS_Notebook_TUF_FX505DY-AS.309 @0x1e9000, Lenovo A285 @0x3bf220, A485 @0x51f420), whose body is empty (Truncated; before #90 they were NotSignedEntry). Fix shape: sign over Entry::header_file_window(blob) and patch at window offset. Note: sign_entry has no blob parameter today; the CLI caller (psptool-cli/src/cmds/sign.rs, replace.rs) holds it.","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:44:25.911386589Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAi88gth/E/BCY/bO18jMrniEi7rTm2sbXp5z8JRbSThsgYmEmPHroAzdQijbct2TrNNf0iIBksO+EHRUch0Y3BA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEn25UOxuoHp7pHmTGAzMRmXD65darmR1dv9XZbxuuZ6Z+JOA0Kxch7ptB5fgcCWywa5YDivXF03RmA6gSerOAY="}
