{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":334,"timestamp":"2026-10-19T20:46:15.347304231Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"f7dd168c-f826-4ad4-adec-395534c077bf","comment_uuid":"6c4a0f29-1df0-4ebf-8e5e-b1b25fa51b89","author":"tLiK","content":"Result: fixed in commit c81670bc (child of 7215971). classify() (entry.rs) parses HeaderFile/KeyStoreFile headers from header_buffer(): the record body, or the 0x100 bytes at its offset when it declares fewer (header_file.py:32-33, key_store_file.py:28-29); Entry::body is unchanged, so the roundtrip is untouched. Entry::header_file_window (body.rs) grows to max(body, 0x100, rom_size). Per entry, all 3 corpus zero-size KVM_IMAGE records now match upstream: ASUS @0x1e9000 signature/verified(60BB); A285 @0x3bf220 and A485 @0x51f420 signature-partial/verified(60BB). The same-offset record that upstream echoes is parsed fresh over the same bytes and reaches the same verdict. Dropped verify_oracle.rs ZERO_SIZE_RECORD_ECHOES (3927/3927, no tolerance). ENTRY_SET_DELTA in decode_verification.rs keeps only the unrelated H12SSW9 cross-ROM echo (+1 signature-failed); tally 4148 = 4147 + 1. Gauntlet: workspace tests 0 failed (ignored tests unchanged: two #48 pins and one doc block), corpus_roundtrip 54/0/0, differential 54/0/0, clippy -D warnings and fmt pass. Still open, tracked elsewhere: our size column shows the directory size 0 where upstream shows buffer_size 0x3100/0xb70, and raw -X writes 0 bytes where upstream writes the rom_size buffer (#101). The echoed record's sectionType is the record's own type where upstream repeats KVM_IMAGE; differential.rs documents this as an equivalent divergence. Spillover: #105 (sign_entry ignores the grown buffer), #106 (pre-existing rustdoc warnings).","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:46:15.341356729Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW