{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":347,"timestamp":"2026-10-19T23:22:30.647914459Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"77177c3c-4f43-4530-8d66-62aff66597e9","title":"Divergence: psptool sign / replace -p pass no IKEK, so the 256 encrypted corpus HeaderFiles cannot be re-signed; upstream get_signed_bytes decrypts with the Zen+ IKEK (header_file.py:286-307)","description":"Spillover from #105. psptool-cli/src/cmds/sign.rs:21 and cmds/replace.rs:59 call sign_entry(.., ikek = None); HeaderEntry::get_signed_bytes then fails NotEncrypted for an encrypted entry (body.rs decode: ikek.ok_or(BodyError::NotEncrypted)). Upstream resign_only signs file.get_signed_bytes() (cert_tree.py:113), whose get_decrypted_body unwraps with get_unwrapped_ikek() = UNWRAPPED_IKEK_ZEN_PLUS unconditionally (header_file.py:286-307). Corpus: 256 signed HeaderFiles are encrypted (reference probe, 241629b). Fix shape: pass Some(Ikek::ZenPlus) in both CLI callers (both files are unrouted: add routes first, R-XLATE-2); psptool-cli/tests/sign_oracle.rs can then include an encrypted control.","priority":"medium","parent_uuid":"525d7258-de71-4087-8d5a-f7dd155266b5","created_by":"tLiK"},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHIGSXm/I3l21IgwLneQej4ZQN5FvpRY30ut8A+nGNH2D7ax/fZcRKQZeAg1e/4LwUoulVsfJvjaVhxpX4IUeww="}
