{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":350,"timestamp":"2026-10-19T23:23:01.018140944Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"8c70f226-69d1-4f16-9468-1e51f93cf14e","title":"Divergence: sign_entry does not refresh a stale header sha256 before re-signing; upstream resign_only rehashes (cert_tree.py:103-110)","description":"Spillover from #105. SignedEntity.resign_only first checks has_sha256_checksum and, when verify_sha256 fails, calls update_sha256 (header_file.py:119-121: _sha256_checksum[:] = sha256(get_checksummed_bytes())) before signing, so a replaced body gets a fresh checksum inside the signed header. psptool-ops/src/sign.rs sign_entry only patches the signature region, so after psptool replace -p the header keeps the old sha256 and the new signature covers it. Unmodified corpus entries are unaffected (their checksum verifies). Fix shape: in sign_entry, when has_sha256_checksum() and the stored digest != sha256(decoded body), patch header[0x20:0x40] (header_file.py:46) before computing the signed bytes, over Entry::header_file_window; pin with a replace-then-sign test.","priority":"medium","parent_uuid":"525d7258-de71-4087-8d5a-f7dd155266b5","created_by":"tLiK"},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGOrdRYIUsybg0FMRtIfDIT2W8yWyWrSQTIcSZOddYUZT/nG3mA2Fhd9bsqF5aqZhr3XVshN09tQCcYiTAaWYw0="}
