{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":353,"timestamp":"2026-10-19T23:23:24.077850409Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"9dd7969e-3f3d-417d-a67a-715c85d241ee","title":"Divergence (latent): sign_entry re-signs a KeyStoreFile with the HeaderFile convention; upstream signs header || key_store and writes at 0x100 + body_size (key_store_file.py:44-51)","description":"Spillover from #105. sign_entry accepts EntryClass::KeyStore but signs HeaderEntry::get_signed_bytes (header || decoded[..size_signed]) and patches signature_bytes (rom_size - signature_len). Upstream KeyStoreFile.get_signed_bytes is header || key_store, key_store = decoded body cut to size_uncompressed when compressed (key_store_file.py:39-42, :50-51), signature at [0x100 + body_size, packed_size) (:44-47, :126-130). Reference probe over the corpus (241629b): all 12 KeyStoreFiles are uncompressed and both conventions give the same signed bytes and signature address, so nothing diverges today; a compressed key store would. Fix shape: for KeyStore use HeaderEntry::get_key_store_signed_bytes (body.rs) and the key_store_signature region (needs a pub accessor whose consumer is sign_entry).","priority":"low","parent_uuid":"525d7258-de71-4087-8d5a-f7dd155266b5","created_by":"tLiK"},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFijJThqY44VSKimuSj4X4ZhtzG3e894fkW2jGutot5B9+q2tWV3QFW8lPtM1v4Vr4W/n+3SjoTkRKozVFWs0Aw="}
