{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":394,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T02:17:13.545460375Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"5de53d47-8827-431f-88a6-8320e361bdbf","title":"Divergence: ls tables center odd padding differently from PrettyTable (extra space goes right; PrettyTable puts it left for even-length text)","description":"PrettyTable _justify('c') (used by upstream psptool.py:68/79 tables and every header row): for odd excess it puts the extra space on the RIGHT when the text has odd length and on the LEFT when even. psptool-ops table.rs render_row always puts it on the right. Example: reference '|  $PSP |' vs ours '| $PSP  |'; header '|         Generation        |' vs ours one space shifted. Spotted while adding multi-line cells to table.rs for #117. Fix shape: mirror PrettyTable's parity rule in Align::Center, regenerate list_micro + psptool-cli synthetic snapshots. Text-only.","priority":"low","parent_uuid":"525d7258-de71-4087-8d5a-f7dd155266b5","created_by":"tLiK"},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGWOatvhPu7I0pHrMzyduIISLJe27VTRMT0ktT0dC9ECOixzQMHq0XUy2SwPMlPNcOqvxVsY+vUoeylhWL77LAw="}
