{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":410,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T03:44:45.670693508Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"2797d073-2ce9-4dd9-932a-f643a2a95c56","title":"Divergence: psptool-py PSPTool() of an input under 8 MiB returns an empty parse; upstream raises ValueError (blob.py:53-54)","description":"Upstream PSPTool 241629b blob.py:53-54:\n    possible_rom_sizes = [32, 16, 8]\n    _rom_size = max(value for value in possible_rom_sizes if value * 1024 * 1024 <= self.buffer_size)\nFor len(rom_bytes) < 8 MiB the generator is empty, so PSPTool(...) and PSPTool.from_file(...) raise ValueError ('max() iterable argument is empty').\npsptool-py never raises: crates/psptool-py/src/tool.rs:137-156 (PSPTool.__new__ -> build -> model::build, model.rs:175-188 scan_fet_candidates/detect_rom_layout) returns a PSPTool whose blob.roms == [].\nLive oracle (reference interpreter, 241629b): sizes 0, 5, 1 MiB, 8 MiB-1 -> ValueError x4; bindings -> len(blob.roms) == 0 x4.\nConsumer impact: PSP-DB pspdb/actions/analyze.py:55-60 wraps PSPTool.from_file in 'except Exception: continue' to skip every non-firmware file of an extracted download; with the bindings every small file (readmes, flash utilities) is appended to parsed_psps and gets a FirmwareFile row plus a 'No ROMs found' warning. psp-etl ingest.py:149-159 records a parse_errors row upstream; with the bindings there is none.\nNot covered by crates/psptool-py/DEVIATIONS.md (item 5 is about malformed firmware nodes, not a missing ROM-size candidate).\nFailing test: crates/psptool-py/tests/divergence.rs::small_input_raises_value_error (case small_input of crates/psptool-py/tests/oracle_divergence.py).","priority":"high","parent_uuid":"525d7258-de71-4087-8d5a-f7dd155266b5","created_by":"tLiK"},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJ7UhB