{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":414,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T03:45:47.109666162Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"cfed9d64-2909-4fbf-9087-3df9ccb35bb2","title":"Divergence: psptool-py sets destination on HeaderFile/PubkeyFile/KeyStoreFile parsed from a BIOS directory; upstream only BiosFile has it (file.py:396-399)","description":"Upstream PSPTool 241629b file.py:259-265 picks PubkeyFile / KeyStoreFile / HeaderFile before falling back to cls(*file_args), and only BiosFile.__init__ stores the attribute (file.py:397-399: 'super().__init__(...); self.destination = self.entry.destination'). So hasattr(f, 'destination') is False for a HeaderFile/PubkeyFile/KeyStoreFile of a BiosDirectory.\npsptool-py: crates/psptool-py/src/file.rs:1461-1463 (init_file, shared by every class): 'if let EntryRecord::Bios(b) = a.record { obj.setattr(\"destination\", b.destination)?; }'.\nLive oracle on H12SSW9.719: reference HeaderFile:False 39, PubkeyFile:False 2; bindings HeaderFile:True 39, PubkeyFile:True 2 (corpus-wide: 1096 HeaderFile + 69 PubkeyFile). Code that uses getattr(f, 'destination', None) to recognise BiosFile-like objects sees a value upstream does not have.\nFailing test: crates/psptool-py/tests/divergence.rs::destination_only_on_bios_file.","priority":"low","parent_uuid":"525d7258-de71-4087-8d5a-f7dd155266b5","created_by":"tLiK"},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQACP77jltE++I59Uv8RN6vTYptVrtwITV/Xt2BWTF7wb538J444sJn9BMtQi5axSM7BEWbRroZ2AKvKb1IyPmQM="}
