{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":416,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T03:46:05.796269716Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"437add46-7714-4f3c-9669-57b286c9709d","title":"Divergence: psptool-py ls() soft_fuse() of an entry with rsv0 >= 0x80000000 prints a wrapped negative i64; upstream prints the 64-bit value (psptool.py:164-165)","description":"Upstream PSPTool 241629b psptool.py:164-165:\n    if file.type == 0xb:\n        info.append(f'soft_fuse({hex(file.entry.offset + (file.entry.rsv0 << 32))})')\non Python ints. rsv0 bits 31:30 are the entry address mode (entry.py:132-134), so a mode-2/3 soft-fuse record has rsv0 >= 0x80000000.\npsptool-py crates/psptool-py/src/listing.rs:293-297:\n    let offset: i64 = entry.getattr(\"offset\")?.extract()?;\n    let rsv0: i64 = entry.getattr(\"rsv0\")?.extract()?;\n    info.push(format!(\"soft_fuse({})\", py_hex(offset + (rsv0 << 32))));\nrsv0 << 32 overflows i64 and wraps.\nInput: ASRock-A520M-HSV-1.31.ROM, first PSP 0x0B entry with rsv0 |= 0x80000000 (in-memory bytearray). Reference ls(): soft_fuse(0x8000000020000001); bindings: soft_fuse(-0x7fffffffdfffffff).\nFailing test: crates/psptool-py/tests/divergence.rs::soft_fuse_listing_is_unsigned.","priority":"low","parent_uuid":"525d7258-de71-4087-8d5a-f7dd155266b5","created_by":"tLiK"},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBM+9HQZy9Kkg1GE3QrM26V9p6MJn+n+9XpZOJ3+Wt+H6H1o0OuB5gMJ62MIFPbCaHmWpp4VRk7Gd/gfoRppuA0="}
