{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":418,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T03:46:47.155095697Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"39fdab98-8c42-447e-b4f2-a335125d7d04","title":"Divergence: psptool-py ls()/ls_files() pad a cell holding tab/CR/VT/FF by character count; prettytable sizes it as wcswidth -1 (psptool.py:200)","description":"HeaderFile.get_readable_magic keeps every string.printable character (PSPTool 241629b header_file.py:155-159), and string.printable includes '\\t\\n\\r\\x0b\\x0c'. psptool.py:200 'print(t.get_string(fields=fields))' renders with prettytable 3.17 (the reference env), whose _str_block_width(val) is wcwidth.wcswidth(...) == -1 for a cell containing such a control character, so the column width ignores the cell and its padding is width+1.\npsptool-py crates/psptool-py/src/listing.rs:26-35 (render widths) and :66-70 (justify) use text.chars().count().\nInput: ASRock-A520M-HSV-1.31.ROM, first HeaderFile of type 0x1 with header magic (+0x10) set to b'A\\tB\\x0b'. Both get_readable_magic() return 'A\\tB\\x0b', but ls() pads the Magic/ID cell differently (reference '|          A\\tB\\x0b |', bindings '|     A\\tB\\x0b |'). Same mechanism for an AGESA string with a tab.\nFailing test: crates/psptool-py/tests/divergence.rs::listing_pads_control_whitespace_like_prettytable.","priority":"low","parent_uuid":"525d7258-de71-4087-8d5a-f7dd155266b5","created_by":"tLiK"},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNNIekqBqW+581FKHquemZM/7BhCwqZYCMBMYGKoSJ+DKWvWdoKYFpBiqIVAWpKOni/DM05gFLt99w3US/s6SA0="}
