{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":420,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T03:47:06.773110850Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"5c2c8d27-0025-4384-b9bd-bf847da32972","title":"Divergence: import psptool does not load psptool.header_file and the other submodules; upstream __init__.py:17 imports them all","description":"Upstream PSPTool 241629b __init__.py:17 'from .psptool import PSPTool' imports psptool/psptool.py, whose imports (psptool.py:22-30: file, directory, header_file, microcode_file, pubkey_file, blob, utils, cert_tree, errors; transitively rom, fet, entry, crypto, key_store_file) register every submodule as an attribute of the package. After a bare 'import psptool' (or 'from psptool import PSPTool'), psptool.header_file.HeaderFile resolves.\npsptool-py crates/psptool-py/python/psptool/__init__.py:9 'from ._native import PSPTool, __version__' imports none of the re-export modules, so psptool.header_file raises AttributeError until something imports it explicitly.\n.design/psptool-py/bindings.md:29-30 (Summary) promises 'isinstance(f, psptool.header_file.HeaderFile)' keeps working with only the dependency swapped; REQ-1 (bindings.md:62-66) cites __init__.py:17-20.\nLive oracle: hasattr(psptool, sub) after 'import psptool' is True for all 15 of psptool, blob, rom, fet, directory, entry, file, header_file, pubkey_file, key_store_file, microcode_file, cert_tree, crypto, errors, utils under the reference, False for all 15 under the bindings.\nFailing test: crates/psptool-py/tests/divergence.rs::import_psptool_loads_submodules.","priority":"medium","parent_uuid":"525d7258-de71-4087-8d5a-f7dd155266b5","created_by":"tLiK"},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLdiOx4EmsIdm3ELrq6GdvMnQfRuFUwC7atQRW327TsI2Ha+Jm073WrU3KPtkbNjoYQTzRkRu4Ov02z9vdn0gw0="}
