{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":422,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T03:48:02.547678261Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"9bfa569a-cc08-4b5e-8fe1-62aafbf6ba50","title":"Divergence: psptool-py entry/directory field setters reject or re-type out-of-range values (entry.py:100-102,178-180; struct.pack setters entry.py:76-164, directory.py:179)","description":"Upstream PSPTool 241629b:\n  entry.py:100-102 (DirectoryEntry.instance setter)   self.flags = self.flags | ((value & 0xF) << 3)\n  entry.py:178-180 (BiosDirectoryEntry.instance setter) self.flags = self.flags | ((value & 0xF) << 4)\naccept any int (the mask drops the excess). The struct.pack setters (type/subprogram/flags/size/offset/rsv0 entry.py:76-126, destination/region_type/flags entry.py:146-164, Directory.count directory.py:174-180) raise struct.error for an out-of-range value.\npsptool-py extracts fixed-width ints before masking: crates/psptool-py/src/directory.rs:381 'fn set_instance(slf, value: u16)', :494 (BIOS), and the u8/u16/u32/u64 setters (directory.rs:116, :349-472) raise OverflowError.\nLive oracle on ASRock-A520M-HSV-1.31.ROM first PSP 0x1 / BIOS 0x62 entries: instance = 0x10013 -> reference flags 24, bindings OverflowError; instance = -1 -> 120 vs OverflowError; BIOS instance = 0x10001 -> 27 vs OverflowError; subprogram = 0x1FF, flags = -1, size = 1<<32, destination = 1<<64, Directory.count = -1 -> struct.error vs builtins.OverflowError (an 'except struct.error' no longer catches).\nFailing test: crates/psptool-py/tests/divergence.rs::entry_setters_match_upstream.","priority":"low","parent_uuid":"525d7258-de71-4087-8d5a-f7dd155266b5","created_by":"tLiK"},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCMSyIDaL2v9nz+IZkjgkV5OTwooWNjCPiIAwNqGLezmUqtSfjmu9fQBRjzTyV6KTZVywOKspAIf51kNS0KQEQU="}
