{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":437,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T04:12:44.158932173Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"3b98f619-1a78-4106-b47d-d7fcffb8c9e6","title":"Divergence: psptool -E on a 64 MiB image with no FET exits 1 'no FET found'; upstream prints nothing / '[]' and exits 0 (psptool.py ls/ls_json)","description":"Bulk differential vs PSPTool 241629b over the psp-etl corpus (1350 ROMs, checkout dcfec1f). sha c248eac28fc5530d018cdbc048221560aab22978b0982297ea55f1d74be3b126 (67109128 bytes = 0x4000108, ARM reset-vector image, no FET at any probed offset). Upstream: stderr 'Warning: Input file is 0x4000108, will assume ROM size of 32M' + 'Warning: Could not find any Firmware Entry Table!', exit 0, -E stdout empty, -E -j stdout '[]'. Ours: 'psptool -E -j -r 0' exits 1 with 'psptool: <path>: no FET (Firmware Entry Table) found', no stdout. This is the only ours-crashed ROM of 1350 (no panics anywhere). Expected: exit 0 with empty ls / '[]' for -j (warning on stderr is fine). Note the sha 412449d3 (128 KB blob that upstream crashes on at blob.py:54) also gives a clean exit-1 error on ours, no panic. Harness: scratchpad diffloop.py.","priority":"medium","parent_uuid":"525d7258-de71-4087-8d5a-f7dd155266b5","created_by":"tLiK"},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQP5jCV+sMFz/ns5XzUiXf4eoreyOo5dgi14+FaL5yuBvknVveV6QQ9SoQgL9hQHTn37WniOosH8IJSRcGFfBVAQ="}
