{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":439,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T04:12:58.253613040Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"7bbbcfff-7683-4b9e-b069-fa2f6c50059f","title":"Divergence: second dir record at a shared offset reports S0I3_DRIVER~0x2d where upstream echoes ANOTHER_FET~0x46 from an earlier directory (likely cache-echo; differential.rs only tolerates size, not type)","description":"Bulk differential vs PSPTool 241629b (checkout dcfec1f), 21/1350 ROMs fail crates/psptool-cli/tests/differential.rs-equivalent projection on the same row. Dir @0x2f9800 (or @0x2f1800 in 6 ROMs) entry idx 23: ours address 0x5c8800 size 0x40000 type S0I3_DRIVER~0x2d (ls -v: magic 00000000); reference address 0x5c8800 size 0x40000 type ANOTHER_FET~0x46. Upstream also lists idx 24 as ANOTHER_FET at the same address; ours lists idx 24 ANOTHER_FET~0x46 and idx 23 S0I3_DRIVER. An earlier directory in the same ROM has ANOTHER_FET~0x46 at 0x5c8800 (ls row 31 of the first /$PSP dir), so this looks like upstream files_by_offset cache echo (file.py:47-54) seeded from that dir, same class as #40/#41/#77, but the size-only dedup tolerance in compare_structure does not cover a type echo, so the test would flag it. Decide: extend the tolerance to type with a seed check (same discriminator as the cross-ROM rule), or treat as real. Example shas: 061aea81bb75330269144e7ee8358c96d3a468c01c83f20d26d07da425adb793, 0d91316defc03abd0aa930521fd674836a896dd5705994d57173d46103ddfb9b, 0f18e9b7343ac0f604b7a2e813dbbd918d160957deec8ebf4782fcd5dd22026a; all 21: dir@0x2f9800: 061aea81 0d91316d 0f18e9b7 210e76f2 2a902489 442f2cfd 828d9a5e 898433e8 bb244ba7 c238f683 d0a2d869 e86aece5 f083965f f916f2ab fd6b914f; dir@0x2f1800: 0f676ccc 4604ce70 50a43479 674c90d9 794b3dcd 7b6843dc. Only the first mismatching row per ROM is recorded by the harness.","priority":"low","parent_uuid":"525d7258-de71-4087-8d5a-f7dd155266b5","created_by":"tLiK"},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lH