{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":456,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T05:40:48.728149167Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"8c783248-2efb-4e78-8cbd-ae679e1c9759","title":"Spillover: BodyError::NotEncrypted reads 'entry is not encrypted (is_encrypted == 0)' when an encrypted entry is decoded without an IKEK","description":"Spotted while fixing #108: before the fix, 'psptool sign' on an encrypted HeaderFile failed with 'entry is not encrypted (is_encrypted == 0)'. psptool-core body.rs decode() maps a missing IKEK for an encrypted entry to BodyError::NotEncrypted (ikek.ok_or(BodyError::NotEncrypted)), the same variant get_decrypted_body returns for a genuinely unencrypted entry, so the message states the opposite of the cause. Fix shape: a distinct BodyError::IkekRequired (or similar) for the missing-IKEK case; callers that match NotEncrypted (cmds/extract.rs single-file -c precondition, extract.rs) keep their semantics. Library-surface change (BodyError variant).","priority":"low","parent_uuid":"525d7258-de71-4087-8d5a-f7dd155266b5","created_by":"tLiK"},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHqyaY+TZ0/vxrfsYBCCGpaPTymJXg99HTX4QgGA914RRIrljzUo77rm2XNgwa6pyKJYAt0/U9+EswyipKDRHQM="}
